(7577831, 1217052, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>When I look upon your photo I think: the city nestled within the hills and mountains. The composition perfectly captures the stacked layers of nature, man, nature, and man again. The nighttime shot shows the juxtaposition of the two more clearly as that the dark rolling hills/mountains contrast greatly with the lights of the city. My only critique on this capture is that the green hue takes away from the photo - making it a straight B&amp;W would further strengthen the contrasts between light and dark as well as the juxtaposition of man and nature.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. When I look upon your photo I think: the city nestled within the hills and mountains. The composition perfectly captures the stacked layers of nature, man, nature, and man again. The nighttime shot shows the juxtaposition of the two more clearly as that the dark rolling hills/mountains contrast greatly with the lights of the city. My only critique on this capture is that the green hue takes away from the photo - making it a straight B&W would further strengthen the contrasts between light and dark as well as the juxtaposition of man and nature.', '2018-07-06 09:47:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7577833, 1217016, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I like how the sunlight bathes the tops of the hills - the play of light and shadow is wonderful here. And nestled within the folds of these rolling hills is a herd of horses which not only add visual interest to the landscape but it also gives the viewer a sense of scale. My one suggestion is that the composition would be stronger and draw the eye in more readily if you cropped closer to the main section of the rolling hills. About 20% off the top and bottom as well as 25% off the left side would then bring the hills into the front and center focus.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I like how the sunlight bathes the tops of the hills - the play of light and shadow is wonderful here. And nestled within the folds of these rolling hills is a herd of horses which not only add visual interest to the landscape but it also gives the viewer a sense of scale. My one suggestion is that the composition would be stronger and draw the eye in more readily if you cropped closer to the main section of the rolling hills. About 20% off the top and bottom as well as 25% off the left side would then bring the hills into the front and center focus.', '2018-07-06 09:58:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7577849, 1215545, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>There are some good leading lines in this street photography shot. The couple holding hands adds some visual interest. One suggestion I have to improve on this photo is to play with the contrasts between light and shadow to make the contrasts in this black and white more dynamic. The midtones and shadows are a bit flat. Increasing contrasts in those areas will make this photo pop more visually.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. There are some good leading lines in this street photography shot. The couple holding hands adds some visual interest. One suggestion I have to improve on this photo is to play with the contrasts between light and shadow to make the contrasts in this black and white more dynamic. The midtones and shadows are a bit flat. Increasing contrasts in those areas will make this photo pop more visually.', '2018-07-06 10:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7577850, 1215903, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Interesting shapes and patterns presented in an unusual angle that does invoke Escher''s style. B&amp;W tones are wonderfully dynamic. I wonder what more one would see if it expanded more in the horizontal region and if it would add to the composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Interesting shapes and patterns presented in an unusual angle that does invoke Escher''s style. B&W tones are wonderfully dynamic. I wonder what more one would see if it expanded more in the horizontal region and if it would add to the composition.', '2018-07-06 10:42:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7577852, 1217231, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Tones, lighting, colors, and details are all great in this streetside shot that showcases the school building on the corner. There is some lovely architectural elements to this school building. One thing that detracts from the composition and cuts across the top portions of the main subject is those power lines. One way you can minimalize the impact those power lines have on your composition is to try to take the shot from a lower angle. I.E. by placing the camera at street level and in a looking upward angle it has the strong possibility of having all or most of the power lines cross the sky rather than cut across the building. An added bonus is that it makes the building ''appear'' taller from the lower angle so it will add to the feel that it is taken from the viewpoint of a small child (which plays well with the picture of the Beck School).</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Tones, lighting, colors, and details are all great in this streetside shot that showcases the school building on the corner. There is some lovely architectural elements to this school building. One thing that detracts from the composition and cuts across the top portions of the main subject is those power lines. One way you can minimalize the impact those power lines have on your composition is to try to take the shot from a lower angle. I.E. by placing the camera at street level and in a looking upward angle it has the strong possibility of having all or most of the power lines cross the sky rather than cut across the building. An added bonus is that it makes the building ''appear'' taller from the lower angle so it will add to the feel that it is taken from the viewpoint of a small child (which plays well with the picture of the Beck School).', '2018-07-06 10:52:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7577856, 1217166, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>A very minimalist and zen photo capturing a dragonfly at rest on a reed. The B&amp;W presentation also makes it a study of light and shadow. I have two suggestions on how to strengthen the zen haiku feel of this photo. First try to keep that light and shadow aspect of it at minimal which means either cropping or, in this case, changing the angle slightly so that dark foliage does not appear in the frame. Second cropping or having the reeds extend out from the bottom left corner will act as leading lines for the eye to follow and be greeted with the sight of the lone dragonfly.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. A very minimalist and zen photo capturing a dragonfly at rest on a reed. The B&W presentation also makes it a study of light and shadow. I have two suggestions on how to strengthen the zen haiku feel of this photo. First try to keep that light and shadow aspect of it at minimal which means either cropping or, in this case, changing the angle slightly so that dark foliage does not appear in the frame. Second cropping or having the reeds extend out from the bottom left corner will act as leading lines for the eye to follow and be greeted with the sight of the lone dragonfly.', '2018-07-06 11:00:21.000000', NULL, 1),
